  "patch_scope": "Explicit CHOS CMake/bmalloc identity;owned-page discard;OS-brokered entropy with bounded retries and fail-closed errors;bounded native Console diagnostics. No local RNG,device fallback or full engine/security/conformance success inferred. Native mutex backoff uses the real scheduled YIELD service,not an unimplemented nanosleep API. Explicit WTF CHOS identity and private pthread selection; separate real native mutex/condition backend,not Unix signals/thread suspension. Native WTF clocks use checked realtime/monotonic services;unavailable clocks fail closed;continuous-time profile does not claim suspend/resume support. Native current-thread register layout and kernel-owned stack discovery;Unix signal-handler declarations excluded on CHOS. Foreign-thread suspend/GC/lifecycle remain unimplemented. Native WTF RandomDevice uses the real OS entropy broker with bounded retries/fail-closed errors;process/page helpers use real native libc services without a racy lazy page cache. Native CPUTime and memory-footprint sources select checked self-only scheduler/resource measurements; blocked time and kernel-root services excluded; no POSIX getrusage stub.; CHOS no-localization profile excludes only optional Int128 std::ostream declarations/formatting;all integer arithmetic,conversions and WTF PrintStream code retained; Native FileHandle uses real owned reads/writes/seek/metadata/conditional durable commit. Unsupported adoption locks rejected;private mapped copies use native anonymous protection,not shared file-backed mmap. Close failure reported before explicit abort.; Native filesystem binds actual owned CHOS I/O and full restartable directory pages. Truncate handles restrict reads across moves;unsupported locks/shared maps reject before mutation. Common native persistence helpers require explicit flush. Current-thread adoption uses native pthread TLS and the upstream two-pass ownership/destruction algorithm;no native Thread creation or foreign GC suspension. Unix signal setup explicitly excluded;config freezing attempts actual native protection and cannot silently succeed through the generic no-op. Shared maps,locks,timestamps,capacity API,descriptor duplication/inheritance and full engine hardening remain open. Native no-JIT ARM64 cache publication fails closed at runtime;JIT-enabled builds retain explicit missing-backend compile failure. CHOS offlineasm selects real ELF GOT relocations,hidden symbols and local labels without defining Linux compatibility. Interpreter metadata/assembly compilation is not JavaScript execution.",
